 "remarks": "Escape the ordinary at this European inspired Greenwich, CT retreat offering exceptional privacy, sweeping river views, and effortless access to the Cos Cob village amenities. Set above the Mianus River, the property features multilevel stone terraces, outdoor fireplaces, mature gardens, and an all season stone gazebo sculpted by the former head designer of the New York Botanical Garden, creating a truly one-of-a-kind outdoor experience. Inside, the completely reimagined, meticulous interior showcases rich hardwood floors, quality moldings, and thoughtful craftsmanship throughout. Versatile living spaces include a chef's kitchen, a dramatic family room with waterview exposure, and luxurious ensuite bedrooms that feel both serene and refined. Large windows and French doors frame the river, enhancing the home's European ambiance and connection to nature. Sidewalks lead to shops, cafes, schools, and the train just five minutes away. This residence blends Old World charm with modern convenience. A rare offering that delivers distinctive character, designer curated grounds, and a lifestyle that stands apart from the standard.",
